cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "transport-fanout: the interest-filtered egress edge"
abstract: >
  One tick of a zone, filtered by interest and sent to the subscribers who should see
  it. The gateway and ingest transports terminate client transport on the way in;
  this is the way out, and a different job -- driven by the zone tick rather than by
  an arriving packet, and doing work per subscriber rather than per connection. The
  nasty path is millions of packets a second, so the entity packet is never CBOR: it
  is the fixed 100-byte XRGridEntityPacket, memcpy and offset reads, version pinned
  per connection.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/transport-fanout"
keywords:
  - interest-management
  - multiplayer
  - zero-copy
  - iceoryx2
references:

  - type: software
    title: "contract-entity-packet: the 100-byte integral fabric entity packet"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/contract-entity-packet"
    notes: >
      The wire format this packs into. `xr_grid_entity_packet.h` is emitted by that
      repository's packet_emit, not written here. Until it was emitted, this repository
      had never compiled: the codec was a file everything included and nobody produced.

  - type: software
    title: "interactor-spatial-oracle: predictive spatial oracle with ghost expansion and SAH proofs"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/interactor-spatial-oracle"
    notes: >
      Emits `predictive_bvh.h`, the other generated header this needs. Both come from
      elsewhere, which is why WEFT_GEN_DIR points at a directory rather than at a path
      inside this tree.

  - type: software
    title: "contract-interest-mgmt: the authority-interest and solve-order hexagon"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/contract-interest-mgmt"
    notes: "Who-sees-whom, which is the filter `src/fanout.cpp` applies per subscriber."

  - type: software
    title: "iceoryx2: zero-copy lock-free inter-process communication"
    authors:
      - name: "ekxide IO GmbH"
    url: "https://github.com/eclipse-iceoryx/iceoryx2"
    notes: "The bus a zone tick arrives on, reached through the contract-bus harness ABI."
